{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"bbc43356-430e-40a9-a14e-41404b640377","agentId":"aa1325351951d62ee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient: read only what you edit; 5 checks; one 400px screenshot; report under 100 words. Your files: NEW cuore/web/systems_routes.py, cuore/web/systems_svg.py, cuore/web/templates/systems.html, cuore/web/templates/_system_badge.html, cuore/web/static/systems.css, cuore/tests/check_systems_page.py; small edits: _vbar.html (Systems tab after Timeline), code.html (system badges with upstream list under the code title), vehicle.html (system badges on open-work cards), timeline_svg.py + timeline_routes.py (an optional \"by system\" lane mode ?lanes=systems grouping bars by system instead of family, reuse existing colours/style grammar), report.html (a \"Systems involved\" section). Do not edit app.py (report include line), api/*, services/*, mes-log-mcp/*.\n\nRepo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; cuore FastAPI + Jinja, phone-first (44px targets; classes at the end of cuore/web/static/cuore.css; status colours red active, amber unverified, green ok, grey stale; dark/light variables); server-rendered SVG only (pattern cuore/web/timeline_svg.py). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. A data agent is building in parallel cuore/services/systems_bridge.py with systems() -> ordered list of {key, label, components, live_channels, maintenance_items, parts, depends_on: [{system, why, confidence, source}]}, systems_for_code(code, description=\"\") -> [{system, role: primary|upstream, confidence, source}], correlate(vin) -> {\"by_system\": [{system, codes, sessions, first, last, status}], \"co_occurrence\": [{a, b, sessions_together, sessions_a, sessions_b, lift, reading}], \"chains\": [{issue, possible_upstream: [{system, why, evidence}]}], \"findings\": [str]}. Develop against a fixture until it lands; import lazily; degrade gracefully.\n\nBuild: (1) /v/{vin}/systems page: top findings; a dependency GRAPH as SVG (systems as rounded nodes in a fixed layout, arrows = depends_on with confidence as line style: solid CONFIRMED/CORROBORATED, dashed SINGLE-SOURCE, dotted UNKNOWN; node fill = status colour from by_system; node badge = code count; a <title> per node/edge; tap a node -> scrolls to its card); a co-occurrence table (system pair, sessions together, lift, reading); \"possible upstream causes\" chains as cards with their evidence and confidence; one card per system: status chip, codes (links), live channels with known-good band notes, maintenance items due, parts, experience links (reuse the `experience_links` and `parts_for` Jinja globals if defined). Legend. Works at 400px (graph scrolls in its container). (2) _system_badge.html: compact chips \"EVAP (primary) · Electrical (upstream?)\" used on code.html and open-work cards. (3) Timeline ?lanes=systems mode and a toggle link. (4) Tests: systems page 200 with graph svg and legend; a dashed/dotted stroke present; code page P0455 shows the EVAP badge; timeline ?lanes=systems 200; no horizontal overflow at 400px (CDP pattern from cuore/tests/check_live_widgets.py, Edge cleanup via _edge_cleanup.py) with one screenshot to the scratchpad. Run + check_timeline_page.py (TestClient part) and check_api.py."},"uuid":"acf29247-7030-4583-9c49-7e2dd153fcb9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:41:44.328Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
