{"parentUuid":"c57c8c75-2e92-491b-af08-033e3967922c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa1325351951d62ee","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfp2AVE47k8c9xZFsP41R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WjR8Qhi1v9LVn4JcrKcd1w","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Built the Systems view end-to-end. New: cuore/web/systems_routes.py, cuore/web/systems_svg.py, cuore/web/templates/systems.html + _system_badge.html, cuore/web/static/systems.css, cuore/tests/check_systems_page.py (16/16 checks pass, incl. 400px screenshot with no overflow, saved to scratchpad/systems_phone.png). Small edits: _vbar.html (Systems tab), code.html/vehicle.html/report.html (badges), timeline_svg.py (+regroup_by_system), timeline_routes.py (+?lanes=systems), timeline.html (Group toggle). Did not touch app.py/api/*/services/*/mes-log-mcp/*.\n\nKey finding: the real cuore/services/systems_bridge.py landed mid-task from the parallel data agent, and its actual shape differs from the brief in two ways I adapted to: systems() returns an ordered dict (key->record), not a list — I normalize it; and status vocabulary is active/cleared_unverified/clean/stale (not active/unverified/ok/stale) — fixtures and CSS-class maps now match exactly. Also live_channels/parts are plain known-good/part keys, not inline dicts, so systems_routes.py resolves them via known_good_bridge.sourced_band and parts_bridge.part for display.\n\nVerified: check_systems_page.py 16/16, check_timeline_page.py 48/48 (incl. companion check_dossier_page.py and check_api.py), check_api.py standalone 96/96 all green. No regressions."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":244850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":254,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WjR8Qhi1v9LVn4JcrKcd1w":{"message":"Built the Systems view end-to-end. New: cuore/web/systems_routes.py, cuore/web/systems_svg.py, cuore/web/templates/systems.html + _system_badge.html, cuore/web/static/systems.css, cuore/tests/check_systems_page.py (16/16 checks pass, incl. 400px screenshot with no overflow, saved to scratchpad/systems_phone.png). Small edits: _vbar.html (Systems tab), code.html/vehicle.html/report.html (badges), timeline_svg.py (+regroup_by_system), timeline_routes.py (+?lanes=systems), timeline.html (Group toggle). Did not touch app.py/api/*/services/*/mes-log-mcp/*.\n\nKey finding: the real cuore/services/systems_bridge.py landed mid-task from the parallel data agent, and its actual shape differs from the brief in two ways I adapted to: systems() returns an ordered dict (key->record), not a list — I normalize it; and status vocabulary is active/cleared_unverified/clean/stale (not active/unverified/ok/stale) — fixtures and CSS-class maps now match exactly. Also live_channels/parts are plain known-good/part keys, not inline dicts, so systems_routes.py resolves them via known_good_bridge.sourced_band and parts_bridge.part for display.\n\nVerified: check_systems_page.py 16/16, check_timeline_page.py 48/48 (incl. companion check_dossier_page.py and check_api.py), check_api.py standalone 96/96 all green. No regressions."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3a299933-f203-4c17-bf21-a5316f7e6c55","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfp2AUuCr6Mv4XvhRD1BK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ace8a209-fe95-4dca-bb53-bc707d86a27a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:58:42.289Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
